.TH CTPOOL_TIMED_SUBMIT_FUTURE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_timed_submit_future \- submit a future task with a relative timeout
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

ccol_retval_t ctpool_timed_submit_future(ctpool pool,
                                         void *(*fn)(void *),
                                         void *arg,
                                         struct timespec *timeout,
                                         ctpool_future **out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates a future and submits it to the pool, waiting at most timeout
for a free slot on a bounded queue. The timeout is a relative duration;
internally it is converted to an absolute deadline using CLOCK_REALTIME.

Passing NULL as timeout is equivalent to ctpool_try_submit_future (no
waiting).

On success *out is set to a new ctpool_future handle with a reference
count of 2 (caller + queued task). The caller must call
ctpool_future_free exactly once when done.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool     Thread pool handle
fn       Task function returning void* (must not be NULL)
arg      Passed to fn (may be NULL)
timeout  Relative duration to wait (NULL = do not wait)
out      Receives the future handle on success; set to NULL on failure
         (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success            - task enqueued; *out set to the future handle.
ccol_invalid_args       - pool, fn, or out is NULL.
ccol_not_enough_memory  - future or task allocation failed.
ccol_not_permitted      - pool is shutting down.
ccol_container_full     - NULL timeout and queue is full.
ccol_timed_out          - timeout elapsed before a slot became free.
ccol_unexpected_failure - clock_gettime returned an unexpected error.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_submit_future (3),
.BR ctpool_try_submit_future (3),
.BR ctpool_future_get (3),
.BR ctpool_future_free (3)
